WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.867
Just this

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.468
afternoon, the

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.335
state legislature

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.704
passed a six week abortion ban.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:05.071
The bill

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:05.905
when signed,

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:06.740
which Governor Ron

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.109
DeSantis has already signaled he will do,

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.543
will make abortion access

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.845
even more difficult

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:12.812
in the Sunshine State,

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.313
which right now

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.382
outlaws abortion after 15 weeks.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.483
And Steve King

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.584
is with us from Saint

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:18.318
Petersburg, Florida.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:18.918
And Steve,

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.787
the current 15 week ban is on

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.789
the books has no exception

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.457
for rape and incest.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:27.360
But this law is a six week ban.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.895
But it would include

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.731
exceptions for rape and incest

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.601
That's right, Jake, but only to a point.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.169
And opponents of this bill say

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.337
it will still make Florida

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.239
one of the most restrictive states

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.041
in the country to get an abortion.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.275
Let me go through

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.910
what this bill actually does.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.045
As you said, it

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.113
bans abortion in most cases

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.882
after six weeks.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.518
There are exceptions for rape, incest

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:53.553
and for victims of human trafficking.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.223
Up until week 15, but after week 15,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.325
the only exceptions are for

00:00:59.325 --> 00:00:59.993
if they're the life

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.194
of the mothers at risk

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:02.695
or if there's a fatal defect.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.630
And even then,

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.898
you have to get two doctors

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.166
to sign off on it.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:08.668
It also prohibits abortion by telehealth

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:09.836
and via email.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.938
So you can't get medication sent to you

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.140
by the Postal Service in Florida.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.375
And then it also requires

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.410
the state Supreme Court

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.311
to take action

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.280
or a change in the Constitution

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.781
before this takes effect.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.883
There's a quirk in Florida's constitution

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.919
that includes a privacy clause.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:26.686
And in the past,

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.888
the state Supreme Court has interpreted

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.458
that to include a right to abortion.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.393
But that Supreme Court

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.027
has shifted

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.895
dramatically in recent years,

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.231
and now Distances has actually appointed

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.766
four of the six members

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.401
and will get to appoint another one soon.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.368
So, Jake,

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.736
where abortion rights advocates

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.105
believe that this Supreme Court

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.673
is likely to overturn

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.474
that privacy

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.341
clause, and

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.075
and really,

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:49.709
at that point,

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.478
it'll be a six week ban in the state

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.378
I just saw

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:56.049
polling suggesting that it's a majority.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:56.850
The American people

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.918
oppose a six week ban

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.954
and that even among Republicans

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.222
it's like 45

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:05.058
45 against it in favor of a six week ban.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.759
I assume that Governor

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:07.827
DeSantis, in addition

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.762
to supporting the principles

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.197
behind this bill, thinks

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:11.865
this is going to help

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:12.932
him politically, perhaps

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.070
Well, certainly if he's going to answer

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.105
the Republican primary for president,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.106
that this is an issue

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:21.508
that is often a litmus test.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.109
He is going to be going up against

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.344
President Donald Trump,

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.312
who appointed several

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.614
Supreme Court justices

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.749
that overturn Roe v Wade.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.117
But like you said,

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.153
this is an issue that Democrats believe

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.687
has given them an advantage

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.722
and given them some

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.557
some tailwinds in recent elections.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:37.991
We just saw

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.791
what happened

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.526
in the Wisconsin

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:40.994
Supreme Court race there

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.896
and a whole bunch of midterm races.

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.664
Abortion loom large as well.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.465
But in Florida,

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:46.766
where Republicans

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.369
control both chambers by a large margin,

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.304
if the census didn't take action,

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.906
it would have been an issue for him

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.174
in the GOP primary.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:54.874
Jake, All right.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:55.975
Steve Cantor now

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.777
in Saint Petersburg, Florida,

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:58.611
thanks so much.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:02:59.812
Attorney General Merrick

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:00.780
Garland is preparing

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.482
to take the fight over the abortion

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.484
pill to the U.S. Supreme Court.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.518
This comes after an appeals

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.554
court declined to ban

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.888
the abortion drug misoprostol

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.023
and in a ruling late last night.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.058
But it made access to the drug

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:12.992
more difficult.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.593
CNN's Joan

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.261
Biskupic is with us to explain.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.262
Joan, what did Attorney

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.564
General Garland have to say

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.331
about bringing this case

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.232
before the Supreme Court?

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.833
And what's the timeline here? Sure.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.901
Good afternoon, Jake.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.870
This is what the attorney general said

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.205
in a statement around noon.

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.372
The Justice Department

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.574
strongly disagrees

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:29.642
with the Fifth Circuit's decision.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.643
We will be seeking

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:31.911
emergency relief

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:32.879
from the Supreme Court

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:35.281
to defend the FDA's scientific judgment

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:36.482
and to protect

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.951
Americans access to safe

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.320
and effective reproductive care.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.354
Now, Jake,

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.989
we haven't seen the full filing yet,

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:43.890
but I imagine

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.391
that the attorney general

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.627
will take strong issue with yet

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:50.163
another court second guessing the FDA's

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:53.032
scientific expertize here.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.167
As you know, though,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.935
the validity of the drug dates

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.804
to the year 2000

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.939
then the restrictions on access

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.775
that are an issue they day to 2016.

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.144
So we've got a lot in place

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.879
and just a reminder

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.749
that this medication abortion protocol

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.585
is the most common form of

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.221
that women are using today in America

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.656
to end their pregnancies.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.524
So there's a lot at stake here.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.692
And you know, it's

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.494
now going back to the Supreme Court

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.162
that completely eliminated

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.964
the constitutional right to abortion

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.432
and left it to the states.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.600
So medication abortion

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.269
is a very crucial part

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.670
of that ability for access

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:31.838
also for women

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.406
who have suffered miscarriages.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:34.274
You rely on. Mr.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.475
President, as we mentioned,

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.043
this all comes after the ruling

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:39.045
from the appeals court last night,

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:40.780
which didn't ban Mr.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.082
Stone
but kept restrictions around the drug.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.251
What are those restrictions? Exactly.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.221
One would be just in terms of

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.156
how how a woman could actually

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:53.359
obtain the drug since 2016,

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.528
there was no longer

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.262
an in-person

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.563
requirement after a woman

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.365
had actually met with physician.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.300
Now we're back to

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:00.900
if this

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.035
if everything stays

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.403
the way
the Fifth Circuit wants it over

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.138
the next 24 hours,

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:05.672
no longer

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.439
could a woman

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.041
get the drug by mail

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.742
after the initial consultation

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:10.476
with a physician.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.277
So that's one thing.

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:11.944
And the second thing

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.314
is the window for availability

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.250
would decrease generally from

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.718
currently ten weeks down

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.420
to seven weeks of pregnancy.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.421
So those are

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:23.423
those are significant access issues

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.891
that would be rolled back

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:27.126
if the Supreme Court does not stop

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:29.262
the effect of the two lower court

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:29.896
decisions.

